{"module":"rights","voice":"female","duration":203.6,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Your rights with police, and after a weaponized call","start":0.0,"end":3.53,"words":[[0.04,0.2],[0.2,0.61],[0.61,0.86],[0.86,1.35],[1.64,1.89],[1.89,2.21],[2.21,2.38],[2.38,3.12],[3.12,3.36]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This is general information about U.S. law, not legal advice, and laws differ by state.","start":4.33,"end":10.31,"words":[[4.38,4.58],[4.58,4.71],[4.71,5.24],[5.24,5.91],[5.91,6.24],[6.24,6.57],[6.91,7.11],[7.34,7.54],[7.54,7.87],[7.87,8.34],[8.57,8.77],[8.77,8.97],[8.97,9.23],[9.23,9.43],[9.43,9.83]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The goal of every encounter is to get home safely; you can challenge what happened later.","start":10.66,"end":15.36,"words":[[10.71,10.83],[10.83,11.07],[11.07,11.19],[11.19,11.43],[11.43,11.91],[11.91,12.03],[12.03,12.15],[12.15,12.33],[12.33,12.57],[12.57,12.99],[13.2,13.32],[13.32,13.5],[13.5,13.98],[13.98,14.16],[14.16,14.52],[14.52,14.88]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Free, detailed guides from the ACLU and others are linked on the Take action page.","start":15.71,"end":20.26,"words":[[15.74,16.0],[16.23,16.69],[16.69,17.02],[17.02,17.28],[17.28,17.42],[17.42,17.68],[17.68,17.88],[17.88,18.14],[18.14,18.2],[18.2,18.53],[18.53,18.66],[18.66,18.8],[18.8,19.06],[19.06,19.39],[19.39,19.78]]},{"el":"h0","text":"If police stop you on the street","start":20.61,"end":22.46,"words":[[20.66,20.81],[20.81,21.19],[21.19,21.5],[21.5,21.65],[21.65,21.8],[21.8,21.96],[21.96,22.34]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Police may briefly stop you if they have “reasonable suspicion” that you're involved in a crime, and may pat down your outer clothing if they believe you're armed (Terry v. Ohio, 1968).","start":23.16,"end":34.61,"words":[[23.21,23.56],[23.56,23.78],[23.78,24.2],[24.2,24.49],[24.49,24.63],[24.63,24.77],[24.77,24.98],[24.98,25.2],[25.2,25.84],[25.84,26.4],[26.4,26.62],[26.62,26.76],[26.76,27.26],[27.26,27.4],[27.4,27.54],[27.54,27.97],[28.22,28.43],[28.43,28.64],[28.64,28.86],[28.86,29.14],[29.14,29.28],[29.28,29.57],[29.57,30.06],[30.06,30.21],[30.21,30.42],[30.42,30.77],[30.77,30.92],[30.92,31.13],[31.13,31.41],[31.41,31.63],[31.98,32.55],[32.8,34.08]]},{"el":"s0","text":"You can ask, “Am I free to go?”","start":34.96,"end":36.78,"words":[[35.02,35.12],[35.12,35.28],[35.28,35.5],[35.69,35.79],[35.79,35.9],[35.9,36.06],[36.06,36.17],[36.17,36.38]]},{"el":"s0","text":"If yes, you may calmly leave.","start":37.13,"end":39.08,"words":[[37.18,37.3],[37.3,37.54],[37.76,37.88],[37.88,38.06],[38.06,38.37],[38.37,38.61]]},{"el":"s0","text":"You have the right to remain silent, but the Supreme Court has said you must say you are using it (Salinas v. Texas, 2013): “I'm going to remain silent.”","start":39.43,"end":50.17,"words":[[39.48,39.63],[39.63,39.85],[39.85,40.0],[40.0,40.3],[40.3,40.45],[40.45,40.89],[40.89,41.49],[41.75,41.98],[41.98,42.13],[42.13,42.57],[42.57,42.8],[42.8,43.02],[43.02,43.24],[43.24,43.39],[43.39,43.69],[43.69,43.91],[43.91,44.06],[44.06,44.14],[44.14,44.51],[44.51,44.66],[44.66,45.26],[45.26,45.48],[45.85,46.38],[46.64,47.53],[47.79,48.02],[48.02,48.39],[48.39,48.54],[48.54,48.99],[48.99,49.58]]},{"el":"s0","text":"About half the states have “stop and identify” laws that require you to give your name when lawfully stopped (Hiibel, 2004).","start":50.52,"end":58.99,"words":[[50.57,50.96],[50.96,51.2],[51.2,51.36],[51.36,51.84],[51.84,52.08],[52.08,52.39],[52.39,52.63],[52.63,53.43],[53.43,53.67],[53.67,53.9],[53.9,54.46],[54.46,54.62],[54.62,54.78],[54.78,55.02],[55.02,55.17],[55.17,55.49],[55.49,55.73],[55.73,56.21],[56.21,56.6],[56.6,57.24],[57.52,58.47]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Searches, cars and your home","start":59.89,"end":62.47,"words":[[59.93,60.68],[61.05,61.38],[61.38,61.7],[61.7,61.91],[61.91,62.34]]},{"el":"s1","text":"You can say, “I don't consent to a search.”","start":63.17,"end":65.98,"words":[[63.22,63.35],[63.35,63.55],[63.55,63.81],[64.04,64.17],[64.17,64.5],[64.5,64.96],[64.96,65.09],[65.09,65.22],[65.22,65.55]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Saying it doesn't stop an officer who has other legal grounds, but it preserves your rights for court.","start":66.33,"end":71.87,"words":[[66.33,66.67],[66.67,66.81],[66.81,67.22],[67.22,67.5],[67.5,67.64],[67.64,67.98],[67.98,68.12],[68.12,68.32],[68.32,68.53],[68.53,68.87],[68.87,69.42],[69.66,69.87],[69.87,70.01],[70.01,70.49],[70.49,70.63],[70.63,70.97],[70.97,71.11],[71.11,71.38]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In a traffic stop, the driver must show a license, registration and proof of insurance when asked.","start":72.22,"end":79.46,"words":[[72.27,72.42],[72.42,72.58],[72.58,73.05],[73.05,73.44],[73.71,73.87],[73.87,74.33],[74.33,74.65],[74.65,74.88],[74.88,75.04],[75.04,75.66],[75.93,76.95],[76.95,77.18],[77.18,77.49],[77.49,77.65],[77.65,78.35],[78.35,78.58],[78.58,78.97]]},{"el":"s1","text":"At home, you don't have to open the door unless officers have a warrant signed by a judge; ask them to slide it under the door or hold it to a window.","start":79.81,"end":87.57,"words":[[79.86,79.99],[79.99,80.3],[80.53,80.65],[80.65,80.97],[80.97,81.16],[81.16,81.28],[81.28,81.6],[81.6,81.73],[81.73,81.85],[81.85,82.17],[82.17,82.55],[82.55,82.74],[82.74,82.86],[82.86,83.24],[83.24,83.56],[83.56,83.75],[83.75,83.87],[83.87,84.25],[84.48,84.66],[84.66,84.85],[84.85,84.98],[84.98,85.3],[85.3,85.42],[85.42,85.68],[85.68,85.8],[85.8,85.93],[85.93,85.99],[85.99,86.31],[86.31,86.43],[86.43,86.56],[86.56,86.69],[86.69,87.13]]},{"el":"s1","text":"An immigration (ICE) administrative warrant signed by an officer, not a judge, does not by itself allow entry into a home.","start":87.92,"end":95.64,"words":[[87.98,88.11],[88.11,88.79],[88.79,89.0],[89.23,90.12],[90.12,90.52],[90.52,90.86],[90.86,91.07],[91.07,91.2],[91.2,91.61],[91.85,92.05],[92.05,92.19],[92.19,92.6],[92.83,93.04],[93.04,93.24],[93.24,93.45],[93.45,93.85],[93.85,94.12],[94.12,94.46],[94.46,94.74],[94.74,94.87],[94.87,95.21]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Recording the police","start":96.54,"end":98.08,"words":[[96.59,97.25],[97.25,97.44],[97.44,97.92]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Several federal appeals courts have recognized a First Amendment right to record police doing their jobs in public, starting with Glik v. Cunniffe (2011).","start":98.78,"end":108.85,"words":[[98.85,99.29],[99.29,99.8],[99.8,100.17],[100.17,100.46],[100.46,100.68],[100.68,101.41],[101.41,101.55],[101.55,101.84],[101.84,102.5],[102.5,102.79],[102.79,102.94],[102.94,103.3],[103.3,103.67],[103.67,103.96],[103.96,104.18],[104.18,104.54],[104.54,104.69],[104.69,105.2],[105.46,105.89],[105.89,106.11],[106.11,106.41],[106.41,106.62],[106.99,107.35],[107.35,108.38]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Keep a safe distance, don't interfere, and say out loud that you're recording if asked.","start":109.2,"end":114.86,"words":[[109.2,109.42],[109.42,109.57],[109.57,109.87],[109.87,110.47],[110.73,111.1],[111.1,111.7],[111.96,112.18],[112.18,112.4],[112.4,112.63],[112.63,112.93],[112.93,113.15],[113.15,113.3],[113.3,113.82],[113.82,113.97],[113.97,114.34]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Many weaponized 911 calls became public only because someone recorded them.","start":115.21,"end":120.44,"words":[[115.26,115.52],[115.52,116.09],[116.09,117.29],[117.29,117.54],[117.54,117.93],[117.93,118.31],[118.31,118.62],[118.62,118.94],[118.94,119.32],[119.32,119.76],[119.76,120.02]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Staying as safe as possible","start":121.34,"end":123.41,"words":[[121.39,121.94],[121.94,122.13],[122.13,122.49],[122.49,122.68],[122.68,123.32]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Keep your hands visible, and don't run, argue or physically resist, even if you believe the stop is wrong.","start":124.11,"end":129.76,"words":[[124.11,124.29],[124.29,124.42],[124.42,124.73],[124.73,125.22],[125.44,125.62],[125.62,125.93],[125.93,126.18],[126.4,126.65],[126.65,126.71],[126.71,127.14],[127.14,127.58],[127.79,128.04],[128.04,128.17],[128.17,128.29],[128.29,128.6],[128.6,128.72],[128.72,128.97],[128.97,129.09],[129.09,129.34]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Tell officers before you reach for anything: “My license is in my back pocket.”","start":130.11,"end":134.44,"words":[[130.13,130.33],[130.33,130.73],[130.73,130.99],[130.99,131.13],[131.13,131.39],[131.39,131.53],[131.53,131.99],[132.23,132.43],[132.43,132.89],[132.89,133.03],[133.03,133.16],[133.16,133.36],[133.36,133.56],[133.56,133.96]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Don't lie or give false documents.","start":134.79,"end":137.0,"words":[[134.85,135.15],[135.15,135.33],[135.33,135.39],[135.39,135.58],[135.58,135.82],[135.82,136.48]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Teach children what to do, and agree on a family plan for who to call.","start":137.35,"end":141.82,"words":[[137.35,137.64],[137.64,138.22],[138.22,138.44],[138.44,138.59],[138.59,138.8],[139.06,139.28],[139.28,139.57],[139.57,139.72],[139.72,139.86],[139.86,140.3],[140.3,140.59],[140.59,140.74],[140.74,140.88],[140.88,141.03],[141.03,141.32]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Remember officer names, badge and car numbers, and witnesses' names.","start":142.17,"end":147.15,"words":[[142.22,142.75],[142.75,143.13],[143.13,143.59],[143.85,144.16],[144.16,144.39],[144.39,144.54],[144.54,145.07],[145.34,145.57],[145.57,146.18],[146.18,146.63]]},{"el":"h4","text":"If someone called the police on you because of who you are","start":148.05,"end":151.02,"words":[[148.1,148.25],[148.25,148.73],[148.73,149.04],[149.04,149.2],[149.2,149.59],[149.59,149.75],[149.75,149.91],[149.91,150.3],[150.3,150.46],[150.46,150.61],[150.61,150.77],[150.77,150.85]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Write it all down as soon as you can: date, time, place, what the caller said, what officers did, names and badge numbers, and witnesses.","start":151.72,"end":160.36,"words":[[151.77,152.03],[152.03,152.16],[152.16,152.3],[152.3,152.56],[152.56,152.69],[152.69,152.89],[152.89,153.02],[153.02,153.15],[153.15,153.42],[153.65,153.98],[154.21,154.54],[154.77,155.17],[155.4,155.59],[155.59,155.73],[155.73,155.99],[155.99,156.25],[156.49,156.68],[156.68,157.08],[157.08,157.34],[157.57,157.9],[157.9,158.1],[158.1,158.37],[158.37,158.83],[159.06,159.26],[159.26,159.85]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Save evidence: your video and anyone else's, photos, and texts.","start":160.71,"end":165.83,"words":[[160.76,161.04],[161.04,161.61],[161.86,162.0],[162.0,162.5],[162.5,162.71],[162.71,163.14],[163.14,163.57],[163.82,164.39],[164.64,164.85],[164.85,165.35]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Request the records: the 911 recording and the call log are usually public records; use the request template in the toolkit.","start":166.18,"end":173.91,"words":[[166.24,166.68],[166.68,166.81],[166.81,167.25],[167.47,167.6],[167.6,168.8],[168.8,169.24],[169.24,169.43],[169.43,169.56],[169.56,169.74],[169.74,169.93],[169.93,170.0],[170.0,170.44],[170.44,170.82],[170.82,171.26],[171.48,171.67],[171.67,171.8],[171.8,172.24],[172.24,172.75],[172.75,172.87],[172.87,173.0],[173.0,173.44]]},{"el":"s4","text":"File a complaint about officer conduct with the department's internal affairs office or your city's civilian oversight board.","start":174.26,"end":181.12,"words":[[174.28,174.56],[174.56,174.7],[174.7,175.32],[175.32,175.67],[175.67,176.02],[176.02,176.5],[176.5,176.71],[176.71,176.85],[176.85,177.55],[177.55,178.03],[178.03,178.38],[178.38,178.66],[178.66,178.73],[178.73,178.87],[178.87,179.22],[179.22,179.77],[179.77,180.33],[180.33,180.61]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Get legal advice: in San Francisco, Oregon and New York, laws let you bring a civil claim against the caller; elsewhere other claims may apply.","start":181.47,"end":190.49,"words":[[181.49,181.7],[181.7,182.04],[182.04,182.53],[182.77,182.91],[182.91,183.12],[183.12,183.88],[184.12,184.54],[184.54,184.75],[184.75,184.95],[184.95,185.23],[185.47,185.68],[185.68,185.89],[185.89,186.03],[186.03,186.31],[186.31,186.44],[186.44,186.79],[186.79,187.14],[187.14,187.55],[187.55,187.69],[187.69,188.04],[188.28,188.7],[188.7,188.9],[188.9,189.32],[189.32,189.53],[189.53,189.94]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Legal aid, the ACLU or the NAACP can help you find a lawyer.","start":190.84,"end":195.5,"words":[[190.89,191.26],[191.26,191.56],[191.82,191.96],[191.96,192.26],[192.26,192.33],[192.33,192.48],[192.48,193.45],[193.45,193.67],[193.67,193.96],[193.96,194.11],[194.11,194.48],[194.48,194.63],[194.63,195.0]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Tell your story, if you want to, on the Stories page and to your lawmakers.","start":195.85,"end":200.55,"words":[[195.9,196.1],[196.1,196.24],[196.24,196.65],[196.89,197.03],[197.03,197.17],[197.17,197.44],[197.44,197.65],[197.89,198.03],[198.03,198.17],[198.17,198.58],[198.58,198.92],[198.92,199.13],[199.13,199.27],[199.27,199.4],[199.4,200.02]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Stories pass laws.","start":200.9,"end":202.66,"words":[[200.93,201.46],[201.46,201.72],[201.72,202.07]]}]}